  "id": "COMPOUND:23600 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Menthol is implicated in the relationship with NCI-H446 through a series of molecular interactions involving 5-Oxobrucine. The evidence suggests that (+)-Menthol acts as a target for 5-Oxobrucine, which in turn targets NCI-H446. This pathway is consistent across three distinct paths, with (+)-Menthol directly linked to Caspase-5 or Microtubule-associated protein 1B, both of which are targets of 5-Oxobrucine. The shared involvement of 5-Oxobrucine as a mediator in the interaction between (+)-Menthol and NCI-H446 indicates a potential mechanism where the compound modulates cellular processes through the activation of Caspase-5 or Microtubule-associated protein 1B, ultimately influencing NCI-H446. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 5-Oxobrucine in mediating the effects of (+)-Menthol on NCI-H446, though the exact cellular mechanisms remain to be fully elucidated.",
